Package: copernicopia
Type: Package
Title: Download Copernicus Marine Data and Append It to Your Own Data
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R:
    person("Benjamin", "Viola", email = "benjamin.viola@utas.edu.au",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: An interactive, step-by-step interface to the Copernicus Marine
    Service. Log in, pick environmental variables from the full Copernicus
    Marine catalogue, choose a product for each, set a region and time period,
    download the matching NetCDF files, and append the values to a data frame
    of locations and times. Uses the official 'copernicusmarine' Python
    toolbox through 'reticulate'.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends:
    R (>= 4.1)
Imports:
    askpass,
    processx (>= 3.5.0),
    reticulate (>= 1.34),
    tools,
    utils
Suggests:
    callr,
    pkgload,
    testthat (>= 3.1.7),
    withr
Config/testthat/edition: 3
SystemRequirements: Python (>= 3.9) with the 'copernicusmarine' package
    (>= 2.0). Installed automatically by 'reticulate' (>= 1.41) or with
    cmems_install().
URL: https://github.com/BMViola/copernicopia
BugReports: https://github.com/BMViola/copernicopia/issues
